\
smoke.micro — architecture neutral smoke workload

Sums k * w[k] over a small array, so the result is a known number for
every host and every backend. Intentionally kept inside the limits of
the i386 backend: at most 5 live virtual registers, the i386 target has
6 allocatable ones, i32 arithmetic only, no floats, no division.

The runner fills an '@N' argument with N / 4 descending i32 words, so
w[k] = n - k and the result is

    sum(k * (n - k)) = n * (n - 1) * (n + 1) / 6

The body is shaped to hit the interesting code selection: the pointer
walk and the counter each become a single instruction.
\

fun checksum
    ptr data
    i32 n
    ret i32
start
    set i32 acc 0;
    set i32 i 0;
    set i32 addr data;

loop:
    set i32 past >= i n;
    if past : done;

    set i32 word $ addr;
    set i32 acc + acc * i word;

    set i32 addr + addr 4;
    set i32 i + i 1;
    goto loop;

done:
    ret acc;
end
